---
import MotionPage from '@/components/MotionPage.astro';
import MotionStage from '@/components/motion/MotionStage.astro';
import MotionUsage from '@/components/motion/MotionUsage.astro';
import MotionOptions from '@/components/motion/MotionOptions.astro';
import MotionTokens from '@/components/motion/MotionTokens.astro';
import Gallery from '@/components/motion/scenes/Gallery.astro';
import { GalleryControls } from '@/components/motion/scenes/GalleryControls';
import { MotionSharedReact } from '@/examples/react/motion-shared.tsx';
import { MotionSharedAngular } from '@/examples/angular/motion-shared.ts';
import MotionSharedSvelte from '@/examples/svelte/motion-shared.svelte';
---
<MotionPage
  slug="shared-elements"
  title="Motion: morph one into another"
  description="Two elements that share a key are one thing for the eye: a thumbnail opens into its detail, and the detail closes back into it."
>
  <MotionStage scene="gallery" label="Live example: Morph one into another" height={544}>
    <Fragment slot="controls"><GalleryControls client:visible size="page" /></Fragment>
    <Gallery heading="h3" />
  </MotionStage>

  <h2>How to use it</h2>
  <p>
    Two elements that carry the same shared key are one thing for the eye. When one of them appears while the other is
    gone, it starts from the other's last place and size and travels to its own. A thumbnail that opens into a detail is
    the typical case: the thumbnail is hidden and the detail shown in the same task.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`<button type="button" data-motion="reflow" data-motion-shared="shot-1">1</button>
<div data-motion="reflow" data-motion-shared="shot-1" hidden>Detail of 1</div>

// Both changes in the same task: the detail morphs out of the thumbnail
thumbnail.hidden = true;
detail.hidden = false;`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    The key is kebab-case. It is given by the attribute, by the <code>shared</code> option of the binding, or by
    <code>shared</code> in a layout definition, where <code>defineShared('hero')</code> returns the name, typed.
  </p>

  <h2>Use it in the frameworks</h2>
  <p>
    React <code>&lt;Motion name="reflow" shared="photo-1"&gt;</code>, Angular <code>udxMotionShared</code>, Svelte
    <code>&#123;&#64;attach motion('reflow', () =&gt; (&#123; shared &#125;))&#125;</code>. The examples mount the
    thumbnail of a photo, or its detail, and not both: the detail takes the place of the thumbnail.
  </p>
  <MotionUsage name="motion-shared" previewHeight={[296, 280]}>
    <MotionSharedReact slot="react" client:visible />
    <MotionSharedAngular slot="angular" client:visible />
    <MotionSharedSvelte slot="svelte" client:visible />
  </MotionUsage>

  <h2>A tab bar that filters</h2>
  <p>
    The filter of the scene is a Udixio tab bar (<code>Tabs</code>). Its indicator slides from the selected tab to the next
    one on the default spatial spring: the component does it, so the scene holds no shared key for it.
  </p>

  <h2>Options</h2>
  <MotionOptions verb="layout" />

  <h2>Timing and tokens</h2>
  <p>A layout moves on the default spatial spring, unless its definition gives it a timing.</p>
  <MotionTokens tokens={['spring.default.spatial']} />

  <h2>Reduced motion</h2>
  <p>
    Under reduced motion, or with <code>--udx-motion: none</code>, the detail opens and closes at once, and the
    indicator of the tab bar moves at once.
  </p>

  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>One live element holds a key at a time. When two elements with the same key are displayed, the second does not morph, and in development an error is reported.</li>
    <li>The last box of a holder is kept for 600 ms after the holder is hidden or removed. An element that arrives after that starts at its own place.</li>
    <li>The two elements do not cross-fade, and the morph does not use the View Transitions API.</li>
    <li>A layout motion applies to HTML elements only.</li>
  </ul>
</MotionPage>
